          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The promise to help is fulfilled when Ms Alvarez retrieves Jun’s book, but Mina’s sketching goal proceeds without a clear transition or emotional payoff.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mina gives up her atlas to help Jun and ends by drawing from his book, though the resolution is mostly a sequence of actions with little elaboration.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000058\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mina’s choice to help Jun leads to his book being retrieved and to her whale drawing, but the brief event-log style limits the payoff.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Jun gets his missing book and Mina draws from her atlas, but the story does not explain how she balances her own goal with her promise to help.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000036\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The choice to help Jun redirects Mina’s sketch to his whale book, giving the sequence a simple resolution, though it lacks a vivid ending.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Ms Alvarez retrieves Jun’s book while Mina keeps her atlas and sketches the moon; the relationship between the promise and her independent goal remains underdeveloped.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000053\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mina chooses to help and ultimately draws a whale, but the repeated action statements make the ending feel more reported than dramatized.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000021\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The missing book is recovered and both original aims are possible, but the sketching sequence does not clearly connect to Mina’s promise to help.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Jun’s book is retrieved and Mina draws the moon, but there is little development beyond the basic problem-and-retrieval sequence.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000048\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mina’s deliberate choice to help Jun changes what she sketches, though the resolution is concise and lacks a concrete emotional beat.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000002\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mina gives up her atlas to help Jun and draws a whale afterward, but the narrative remains a plain sequence rather than a fully developed scene.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mina’s choice leads from Jun’s missing book to a whale drawing, with a clear outcome but little detail or emotional closure.\",\"group_id\":1}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":2,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All twelve stories share the same library problem: Jun’s whale book is missing, and Ms Alvarez retrieves it from a high shelf with a ladder. The only material branch is whether Mina keeps her moon-sketch plan (s000014, s000023, s000017, s000021, s000034) or returns the atlas and draws a whale after helping Jun (s000028, s000058, s000036, s000053, s000048, s000002, s000057). Most differences are small wording or action-order changes, so this sample shows little plot or language variety; it does not establish diversity across the whole generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Mina wants to sketch the moon and promises to help Jun find his missing whale book; Ms Alvarez retrieves the book, while Mina keeps her atlas and draws the moon.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"Mina puts aside her moon-sketch plan to help Jun recover his missing whale book, then uses his book to draw a whale.\"}]}",
